<article class="env-definition" id="0999">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0999">Definition <span data-tag="0999">52.6.4</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}$ be a sheaf of ideals. Let $K \in D(\mathcal{O})$. We say that $K$ is <em>derived complete with respect to $\mathcal{I}$</em> if for every object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ and $f \in \mathcal{I}(U)$ the object $T(K|_ U, f)$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ is zero. </p>
</article>